@title The Wheel of Dubious Fortune
@start before the show

[[]]:
@transition fade
{{!--
    The Wheel of Dubious Fortune: a game show that shows off as much of Squiffy as it can.

    This file has the start, the wheel, the commercial break, the final round and the endings.
    Each round is in a file of its own in rounds/, and squiffy.json adds the side panel, the
    Prizes and How to play buttons, and the player's settings. studio.css is the studio.

    The theme tune, sounds/theme.mp3, is by Keehar.
--}}
{{!-- Push Hank too far, and the show's over, wherever you are --}}
{{#if patience <= 0 and not (at (array "Hank walks off" "Ending"))}}{{goto "Hank walks off" after="1.5s"}}{{/if}}

[scoreboard]:
{{#if player_name}}## {{player_name}}{{/if}}

**Score:** {{score}}

**Round:** {{#if round > 0}}{{round}} of {{rounds_tonight}}{{else}}Warm-up{{/if}}

**Hank's patience:** {{#if patience > 0}}{{#each (range 1 patience)}}❤️{{/each}}{{else}}💔{{/if}}
_{{#if patience >= 3}}Cheerful{{else if patience = 2}}Strained{{else if patience = 1}}Brittle{{else}}Gone{{/if}}_

[prizes]:
{{#each prizes}}
- {{this}}
{{else}}
You haven't won anything yet. Hank says that's "very on brand for this show".
{{/each}}

[how to play]:
Spin the wheel, play the round it lands on, and win as many points as you can. Three rounds, then the final question.

Be nice to Hank. He's had a long day, and when his patience runs out, so does the show.

**Studio lights** and **Timed rounds** are in the Settings. Turn off timed rounds to take as long as you like.

[[before the show]]:
@set score = 0
@set round = 0
@set patience = 3
@set prizes = []
@set rounds_tonight = 3
@set wheel = ["General Knowledge", "Beat the Clock", "Professor Boom's Lab", "The Mystery Box", "The Audience Decides"]
@set tonight = (slice (shuffle wheel) 0 rounds_tonight)
The studio is dark. A sign above the stage says ON AIR, but it isn't lit yet. Somewhere, someone is testing a microphone: "One, two. One, two. Is this thing... it is? Oh."

"Tonight's recording is about to begin," says a voice. "Please switch off your phones, and laugh when the sign tells you to."

[[Take your seat]](intro)

[[intro]]:
@music sounds/theme.mp3
**{{#animate "typewriter" interval=120}}WELCOME TO...{{/animate}}**

# {{#animate "toast" interval=250}}THE WHEEL OF {{#style "sway"}}DUBIOUS{{/style}} FORTUNE!{{/animate}}

{{#animate "fadeIn" duration=1500}}
The studio lights flicker. {{#if settings.lights = "Budget"}}Most of them stay off. Someone has taped a torch to a broom handle.{{else}}A thousand bulbs blaze into life, and three of them explode.{{/if}} A man in a sequined jacket stumbles onto the stage, holding his cue cards upside down.

"Hello, and welcome! I'm your host, Chuck Wheelsworth!" He squints at the cards. "No, wait. I'm Hank Spinneroni. Definitely Hank."

The studio audience (three people and a cardboard cutout) applauds uncertainly.

"And YOU are tonight's lucky contestant! What's your name?"

<input type="text" data-attribute="player_name" data-section="contestant" placeholder="Your name" required minlength="2" maxlength="24">

[[That's me!]](contestant)
{{/animate}}

[[contestant]]:
@music stop
@sound sounds/applause.mp3
@set player_name = (capitalise player_name)
{{#if (lower player_name) contains "hank"}}
"Another Hank!" Hank clutches his chest. "There can only be one, {{player_name}}. We'll settle this later. Possibly with swords."
{{else if player_name.length > 12}}
"{{player_name}}! That's a lot of name. We'll need a bigger name badge." A stagehand starts writing on a second badge.
{{else}}
"Welcome, {{player_name}}! Or as I like to call you... {{player_name}}!"

Hank waits for a laugh. None comes.
{{/if}}

{{embed "motto"}}

"Tonight, the wheel will choose your fate {{rounds_tonight}} times, from {{wheel.length}} exciting categories: {{join wheel ", " " and "}}. Then it's the final question, for double or nothing! Now, {{#animate "continue" style="wave"}}let's spin...{{/animate}}"

{{#animate "typewriter"}}THE WHEEL OF DUBIOUS FORTUNE!{{/animate}}

{{#animate "fadeIn"}}[[Spin the wheel!]](spin){{/animate}}

[[motto]]:
"Remember our motto: _{{random (array "Whose Fortune Is It Anyway? (Legally, Ours)" "Spin to Win! (Winning Not Guaranteed)" "It's Not Gambling If There's a Wheel")}}_"

[[spin]]:
@inc round
@set spins = 0
@set landed = (first tonight)
@set tonight = (slice tonight 1)
{{#if round = 1}}A rusty wheel descends from the ceiling on a fraying rope, wobbling dangerously.{{else}}The wheel creaks back down from the ceiling. It's wobbling more than before.{{/if}}

Hank gives it a mighty heave. It turns with a noise like a shopping trolley hitting a pothole:

{{!-- Every 140ms, the wheel shows another category, until it lands. The links to the rounds are in
    a section of their own, embedded when it lands, so --check can see that every round is reachable --}}
{{#every 140}}{{inc "spins"}}{{#if spins >= 16}}{{stop}}{{sound "sounds/ding.mp3"}}{{#style "wheel"}}**{{upper landed}}!**{{/style}}

{{embed "play the round"}}{{else}}{{#style "wheel"}}{{random wheel}}...{{/style}}{{/if}}{{/every}}

[[play the round]]:
{{#if landed = "General Knowledge"}}[[Let's play!]](General Knowledge){{/if}}
{{#if landed = "Beat the Clock"}}[[Let's play!]](Beat the Clock){{/if}}
{{#if landed = "Professor Boom's Lab"}}[[Let's play!]](Professor Boom's Lab){{/if}}
{{#if landed = "The Mystery Box"}}[[Let's play!]](The Mystery Box){{/if}}
{{#if landed = "The Audience Decides"}}[[Let's play!]](The Audience Decides){{/if}}

[[next round]]:
{{#if round = 1}}
"And we're off!" Hank checks his watch. "Wait. Is that the time? We'll be right back after these messages!"

[[Cut to the adverts]](commercial break)
{{else if round < rounds_tonight}}
Hank shuffles his cards. "Round {{= round + 1}}, {{player_name}}! Are you ready?"

[[Spin the wheel!]](spin)
{{else}}
The wheel retracts into the ceiling, shedding bolts.

[[On to the final question]](final question)
{{/if}}

{{!-- Commercials: the screen slides away to the left, and the advert slides in from the right --}}
[[commercial break]]:
@clear
@leave slide-left
@transition slide-left
@class advert
@sound sounds/fanfare.mp3
{{#style "advert-card"}}
## Are YOUR wheels dubious?

Try **SPINNERONI'S WHEEL WAX**, the wax that's {{#style "flicker"}}almost legal{{/style}} in {{random (array "seven" "eleven" "nearly four")}} countries!

_"I use it on my wheel, and on my hair!"_ (Hank Spinneroni, paid spokesman)

Side effects may include spinning, dizziness, and spontaneous game show appearances.
{{/style}}

While the adverts run, you could {{saves text="save your game"}}, or {{settings text="adjust the studio lights"}}.

+++Back to the show!
@clear
@leave slide-left
@transition slide-left
"And we're back! Round 2, {{player_name}}!"

[[Spin the wheel!]](spin)

[[final question]]:
@class final
@music sounds/theme.mp3
The studio lights go red. {{#if settings.lights = "Budget"}}(Somebody has put a red sock over the torch.){{/if}} Dramatic music plays. Somebody backstage is humming it.

{{#animate "typewriter"}}THE FINAL QUESTION{{/animate}}

"This is it, {{player_name}}! You have **{{score}} points**, and this question is worth... {{#animate "toast"}}DOUBLE OR NOTHING!{{/animate}}"

The audience gasps. The cardboard cutout gasps too (the air conditioning came on).

"Here's your final question:"

{{#embed "cue card" points="Double or nothing"}}**What is the name of your host?**{{/embed}}

<input type="text" data-attribute="final_answer" data-section="final answer" placeholder="Your final answer" required>

[[That's my final answer]](final answer)

[[final answer]]:
@music stop
"{{final_answer}}," Hank repeats slowly. He leans in. The audience leans in. The cardboard cutout leans in, and has to be propped up again.

"Is that your... final... answer?"

[[It is]](the verdict)

[[the verdict]]:
{{#if (lower final_answer) contains "hank"}}
{{sound "sounds/ding.mp3"}}
"CORRECT! I AM HANK SPINNERONI! Probably!"

{{set "score" score * 2}}
{{#animate "toast"}}SCORE DOUBLED!{{/animate}}
{{else if (lower final_answer) contains "chuck"}}
{{sound "sounds/buzzer.mp3"}}
"That was my FIRST name! The WRONG first name! But you remembered SOMETHING!"

{{inc "score" 50}}
"Fifty points, for listening at the start. That's more than my agent does."
{{else}}
{{sound "sounds/buzzer.mp3"}}
Hank stares at you. A vein throbs in his forehead.

"It's HANK. My name is HANK. I said it at the START."

{{#if patience >= 2}}He takes a deep breath. "But you've been a delight, so I'm not taking your points away. That's the real double or nothing: I'm doing nothing."{{else}}{{set "score" 0}}"Double or nothing, {{player_name}}. You get the nothing."{{/if}}
{{/if}}

[[See how you did]](Ending)

{{!-- The endings --}}
[[Ending]]:
@clear
@leave zoom
@transition zoom 0.8s
@music sounds/theme.mp3
@end
@set counted = 0
@set step = (max 1 (floor (score / 15)))
# Final score: {{#every 60}}{{set "counted" (min (counted + step) score)}}{{counted}}{{#if counted >= score}}{{stop}}{{/if}}{{/every}}

{{#if score >= 600}}
{{sound "sounds/fanfare.mp3"}}
{{#animate "toast"}}GRAND CHAMPION!{{/animate}}

Balloons fall from the ceiling. Confetti explodes. Professor Boom bursts out of the trapdoor to set off celebratory fireworks (indoors, against regulations).

Hank hands you an oversized novelty cheque. It bounces.

"{{player_name}}, you're our GRAND CHAMPION! You've won fame, glory, and whatever prizes we can legally give you once the lawyers have watched the tape!"

The audience carries you out on their shoulders. The cardboard cutout leads the parade.

**THE END: Grand Champion**
{{else if score >= 250}}
{{sound "sounds/applause.mp3"}}
{{#animate "toast"}}WINNER!{{/animate}}

"That's... actually pretty good!" Hank shakes your hand, then checks it's still got all its rings.

A stagehand gives you a gift basket: one (1) cheese, a voucher for 10% off at a shop that closed in 2019, and a sincere thank-you note from Hank.

"Come back any time! Assuming we're not cancelled!"

**THE END: Winner**
{{else}}
Hank looks at his cards. He looks at you. He looks at the audience.

"You know what? You showed up. You tried. And isn't that what really matters?"

{{embed "motto"}}

"No, actually, points are what matter. But good effort!"

He gives you a single balloon. It's already deflating.

**THE END: Participant**
{{/if}}

{{#if prizes.length}}You take home: {{join prizes ", " " and "}}.{{/if}}

{{restart text="Play again"}}

[[Hank walks off]]:
@clear
@leave rumble
@transition fade 1s
@class lights-out
@music stop
@sound sounds/buzzer.mp3
@end
Hank puts down his cue cards, very neatly, one on top of the other.

"No," he says. "No, I don't think so."

He takes off the sequined jacket, folds it over his arm, and walks off the set. A door slams somewhere. A moment later the studio lights go out, {{#style "flicker"}}one by one{{/style}}.

In the dark, the cardboard cutout falls over.

**THE END: Off Air**

You had {{score}} points. You'll never know what they were worth.

{{restart text="Try again, and be nicer to Hank"}}

{{!-- Used by every round: the question, written on one of Hank's cue cards --}}
[[cue card]]:
{{#style "cue-card"}}
{{content}}

_{{points}}_
{{/style}}
